cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use EUR-LexRD in your research, please cite both the dataset
  (DOI: 10.48804/TK4IER) and the accompanying paper (DOI: 10.18653/2026.nllp-1.11).
type: dataset
title: The EUR-Lex Retrieval Dataset
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-07-28

authors:
  - family-names: Koolen
    given-names: Christof
    affiliation: KU Leuven, Centre for IT & IP Law
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2210-6821

abstract: >-
  The EUR-Lex Retrieval Dataset (EUR-LexRD) is an
  evaluation benchmark for long-form similar case retrieval based on the case
  law handed down by the Court of Justice of the European Union (CJEU). The
  EUR-LexRD contains 20,697 English CJEU judgments published between 1954 and
  2025. All cases are enriched with metadata and a case summary and have been
  segmented into six sections (e.g., legal context, facts, and reasoning). Each
  judgment also details outgoing citations to other European Case Law
  Identifiers.

  The evaluation set features 100 query cases and a seeded candidate pool
  created with seven different retrieval strategies. The resulting benchmark
  consists of 12,365 query-candidate pairs, which were human-annotated by nine
  legal experts on a four-tiered relevance scale in order to establish a
  high-quality gold standard. The dataset's features, namely the long document
  length and section segmentation, present new hurdles for retrieval and
  reranker models.

  The EUR-LexRD is intended as a resource to advance the field of legal
  information retrieval by (i) making it possible to compare lexical, dense,
  hybrid and long-document retrieval strategies and (ii) supporting the
  fine-tuning of existing encoder or reranker models. The EUR-LexRD is released
  under a CC BY 4.0 license.

keywords:
  - legal information retrieval
  - similar case retrieval
  - legal case retrieval
  - Court of Justice of the European Union
  - CJEU
  - EUR-Lex
  - long-document retrieval
  - section-aware retrieval
  - natural legal language processing
  - legal NLP

